= Computational complexity — Technical =

== Resource bounds ==
For machine M and input length n, complexity functions can bound:

<pre>
T_M(n) = time
S_M(n) = space
</pre>

under a specified computational model.

== Classes ==
Examples include:

<pre>
P      = deterministic polynomial time
NP     = nondeterministic polynomial time / polynomial-time verifiability
PSPACE = polynomial space
EXP    = exponential time
</pre>

Precise definitions depend on encoding and machine model but are robust under standard polynomially related models.

== Reductions ==
Polynomial-time reductions compare problem difficulty and define hardness/completeness.

If A reduces to B efficiently, an efficient solver for B yields one for A.

== Beyond worst case ==
Average-case, randomized, parameterized, fine-grained, communication, circuit, streaming and distributed complexity expose resource dimensions hidden by classical worst-case time.

